---
title: The record
permalink: /record/
description: Every research report, the briefing, and every model response from the drafting and review of the instruments, attributed to its author, model and lab.
---
<p>The record holds the briefing and prompts put to the reviewing models and the drafting record of every revision. Each drafting record consolidates the reviewing models' responses for that round — what each contributed, what was declined and why, the disagreements that remain — and the drafter's own position. Each file is served exactly as uploaded, attributed to its author (for a model, its name and maker), and hashed; the drafting records are kept under <code>/canonical/</code> and are listed here so that they can be read. Nothing is edited after upload; a correction is a new file. <strong>Not in the repository:</strong> the raw response files returned by each model, the research reports the records cite, and the drafting record for Charter revision 8.</p>
{% if record.items.length == 0 %}
<p class="notice" role="note"><strong>The record is not yet in this repository.</strong></p>
{% else %}
{% for round, items in record.byRound %}
<h2>{% if round == 'unassigned' %}Not a review round (drafter's records){% else %}Review round {{ round }}{% endif %}</h2>
<table>
  <thead><tr><th scope="col">Document</th><th scope="col">Kind</th><th scope="col">Author / model</th><th scope="col">Maker / lab</th><th scope="col">Date</th></tr></thead>
  <tbody>
  {% for it in items %}
  <tr><td><a href="{{ it.url }}">{{ it.title }}</a></td><td>{{ it.kind }}</td><td>{{ it.author }}</td><td>{{ it.maker or '—' }}</td><td>{{ it.date | isoDate or '—' }}</td></tr>
  {% endfor %}
  </tbody>
</table>
{% endfor %}
{% endif %}
